{0 Logging}

Standard output and standard error of the OCaml program reach the Workers logs.
Use [wrangler dev], [wrangler tail] or the dashboard to read them.

{@ocaml[
let handler _req _env _ctx =
  print_endline "request received";
  Printf.printf "answering with %d" 200;
  prerr_endline "this goes to the error log";
  Workero.Response.text "ok\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

Workero flushes standard output and standard error when a {!Workero.serve} or
{!Workero.scheduled} handler ends, also when it raises. [print_string] and
[Printf.printf] need no newline and no [%!].

Output written after the handler ends, for example from a function given to
{!Workero.Context.wait_until}, stays in the buffer until the next handler ends.
Flush it with [flush stdout] or [%!].

{1 Console}

{!Workero.Console} writes to the global [console]. Each call is one log entry
with a level: [log], [info], [warn], [error] or [debug]. It needs no flush.

{@ocaml[
let handler _req _env _ctx =
  Workero.Console.info "request received";
  Workero.Console.warn "disk is almost full";
  Workero.Response.text "ok\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}
